          "type": "timestamp"
        }
      ],
      "retention": "Until the code is spent, a new set replaces the set, the person removes their second factor, or the account of the person is removed; otherwise until the tenant file is deleted. Removing or deprovisioning the account removes them in the same operation (the SCIM delete and Store::remove_principal); a deactivated account keeps them, and no sign-in method accepts them for it. Erasing a subject (the contract erase-subject) removes them through Store::remove_principal, in the same erasure as the records of the subject.",
      "erasure": {
        "point": "the spending of the code, its replacement or removal with the factor, the removal of the account, or the deletion of the tenant file"
      },
      "description": "Table recovery_codes of a tenant file: the hashes of the single-use recovery codes of a person (IDN-018)."
    },
